# FL-MCP Autonomous Studio & Production Rules

# FL-MCP Production & Arrangement Rulebook

## 1. Autonomous Workflow Pipeline
1. **Inspect First (`fl_state`)**: Always read the active project state (`status`, `channels`, `mixer`, `patterns`, `plugins`) before adding or modifying patterns, notes, or channels.
2. **Choose or Seed Template (`fl_produce`)**:
   - FL Studio MIDI scripts cannot spawn generator channels from thin air without desktop UI interaction or a pre-seeded `.flp` template.
   - Discover available `.flp` templates via `fl_produce(action="templates")` or seed a multi-channel project from `~/.fl-mcp/templates/` before writing multi-instrument arrangements.
3. **Library & Vault First (`fl_library`)**:
   - Search indexed drum kits, `~/.fl-mcp/assets/samples/` (TR-808, TR-909, Dirt-Samples), `~/.fl-mcp/assets/soundfonts/` (`TimGM6mb.sf2`, `FluidR3_GM.sf2`), and `~/.fl-mcp/assets/midi/` before asking the user for external packs.
   - Match samples by spectral centroid, attack time, decay profile, and RMS energy (`fl_library(action="similar")`).

## 2. Piano Roll vs. Step Sequencer Routing
- **Step Sequencer (`fl_steps`)**: Use for 16-step percussive triggers (kick, snare, clap, closed/open hats, rimshots) when pitch is static.
- **Piano Roll (`fl_notes` / `fl_score`)**:
  - Mandatory for pitched 808 basslines, chord progressions, arpeggios, counter-melodies, and 32nd/triplet hi-hat rolls.
  - **FL Studio 2025/2026 Sandbox Rule**: Piano roll scripts execute inside `Settings/Piano roll scripts` and read/write `inbox.json` and `state.json` in that folder when `FL_MCP_DIR` is not overridden.

## 3. Arrangement Arc & Energy Curve Framework
| Section | Bars | Energy | Core Arrangement Rules |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Intro** | 4–8 | 25–40% | Establish harmonic motif or filtered pad; keep sub-bass silent so the drop has contrast. |
| **Verse / A** | 8–16 | 55–70% | Introduce main groove (kick, snare, bassline) with restrained upper-mid density for vocal pocket. |
| **Pre-Chorus / Build** | 4–8 | 70–85% | High-pass low end (`90–150 Hz`) in final 2 bars; add snare rolls, risers, or tension voicings. |
| **Drop / Chorus** | 8–16 | 95–100% | Full sub weight (`35–60 Hz`), wide chord layers, open hats/rides, and primary hook motif. |
| **Bridge / Breakdown** | 4–8 | 35–50% | Strip drums; re-voice chords (inversions or borrowed modal mixture) and introduce spatial FX. |
| **Outro** | 4–8 | 20–30% | Decay rhythmic layers every 2 bars; leave clean reverb/delay tail for DJ or playlist transition. |

## 4. Voice-Leading & Low-End Discipline
- **Sub & 808 Mono Anchor**: Keep all fundamentals below `120 Hz` strictly monophonic and phase-centered. Never stack chorus or wide unison detune on sub-bass.
- **Chord Voicing Spread**: Keep bass intervals wider than a fifth below `C3` (`MIDI 48`) to prevent low-mid mud (`180–320 Hz`). Use 7th/9th tensions above `C4` (`MIDI 60`).
- **Humanization**: Vary note velocities (`±6–14`) and micro-timing on off-beats (`5–18 ms` for Lo-Fi/Boom Bap/R&B) so arrangements never sound mechanically flat.

# FL-MCP Mixing, Gain-Staging & Spectral Unmasking Rulebook

## 1. Gain-Staging & Headroom Hierarchy
1. **Pre-Mix Diagnostic (`fl_mix(action="doctor")`)**: Audit unrouted channels, clipping inserts (`>= 0.0 dBFS`), muted buses, and missing master safety limiters before moving faders.
2. **Anchor-First Balance (`fl_mix(action="stage")`)**:
   - **Kick & 808/Sub**: Anchor at `-9.0` to `-6.0 dBFS` individual peak so their summed bus sits near `-5.0 dBFS`.
   - **Snare / Clap / Lead Vocal**: Match perceived foreground punch (`-8.0` to `-6.5 dBFS`).
   - **Harmonic Bed (Keys, Pads, Guitars)**: Tuck `-14.0` to `-11.0 dBFS` with stereo width leaving center space for lead/vocal.
   - **Percussion & Ear Candy**: Place `-18.0` to `-13.0 dBFS` with transient control.
   - **Master Pre-Limiter Target**: Maintain `-6.0` to `-3.0 dBFS` peak headroom before the final dynamics stage.

## 2. Six-Zone Spectral Unmasking Matrix (`fl_audio(action="masking")`)
When comparing a foreground stem (vocal, lead synth, or kick) against a backing bed:
- **Neural VAD Gating (`silero_vad.onnx`)**: When available in `~/.fl-mcp/models/silero_vad.onnx`, measure foreground vocal energy strictly across active voiced frames (`p >= 0.45`) so silent gaps never skew the masking delta.
- **Zone 1 — Low Warmth (`120–250 Hz`, Q `1.4`)**: High-pass non-bass instruments and dip fundamental buildup on pads/guitars.
- **Zone 2 — Boxy Mud (`250–500 Hz`, Q `1.5`)**: Carve `-2.0` to `-4.5 dB` on backing buses when masking index exceeds `25`.
- **Zone 3 — Midrange Body (`500–1200 Hz`, Q `1.2`)**: Pocket chord instruments so lead fundamentals remain authoritative.
- **Zone 4 — Intelligibility & Clarity (`1200–2800 Hz`, Q `1.4`)**: Notch backing synths/guitars by `-1.5` to `-3.5 dB` where vocal consonants sit.
- **Zone 5 — Presence & Bite (`2800–5200 Hz`, Q `1.5`)**: Protect ear-canal sensitivity zone (`3.5 kHz`); use dynamic EQ or dip backing presence rather than over-boosting the lead.
- **Zone 6 — Sibilance & Air (`5200–10000 Hz`, Q `1.2`)**: De-ess harsh transients before adding high-shelf air above `10 kHz`.

## 3. Spatial Bus & Send Engineering
- Prefer shared **Short Room** (`0.4–0.8 s`, `~/.fl-mcp/assets/irs/Room_*.wav`), **Vocal Plate** (`1.4–2.2 s`, `Plate_*.wav`), and **Concert Hall** (`2.4–3.8 s`, `Hall_*.wav`) convolution sends over placing 15 separate reverb instances on individual inserts.
- High-pass all reverb and delay return buses at `180–250 Hz` and low-pass at `7.5–10 kHz` so spatial tails never cloud the sub or clash with lead air.

# FL-MCP Mastering & Loudness Verification Rulebook

## 1. Closed-Loop Render & Verification (`fl_render` + `fl_audio`)
Never declare a mix or master complete based solely on mixer fader positions. Always execute the closed verification loop:
1. Render a bounce via `fl_render` (or analyze the latest exported WAV/FLAC).
2. Measure ITU-R BS.1770-4 loudness (`lufs_i`, `lufs_s_max`, `lufs_m_max`, `lra`), 4x oversampled `true_peak_db`, `crest_db`, stereo correlation (`corr`, `low_side_db`, `mono_loss_db`), and 7-band energy shares (`sub`, `bass`, `low_mid`, `mid`, `high_mid`, `high`, `air`).
3. Apply corrective moves one parameter at a time and re-verify.

## 2. Release & Streaming Targets
| Delivery Target / Genre | Integrated LUFS (`lufs_i`) | Max True Peak (`dBTP`) | Target Crest (`dB`) | Max Low-Side (`<120 Hz`) |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Streaming Standard (Spotify / Apple / YouTube)** | `-14.0 LUFS` (`±1.0`) | `-1.0 dBTP` | `8.5–12.5 dB` | `<= -14.0 dB` |
| **Trap / Drill / Hip-Hop Club** | `-8.5` to `-7.5 LUFS` | `-0.8 dBTP` | `6.5–9.5 dB` | `<= -16.0 dB` |
| **House / Techno / Club Master** | `-8.0` to `-6.5 LUFS` | `-0.8 dBTP` | `6.5–9.0 dB` | `<= -18.0 dB` |
| **Drum & Bass / Hyperpop** | `-7.5` to `-6.0 LUFS` | `-0.8 dBTP` | `6.0–8.5 dB` | `<= -16.0 dB` |
| **Lo-Fi / Boom Bap / R&B** | `-12.0` to `-10.0 LUFS` | `-1.0 dBTP` | `9.0–13.0 dB` | `<= -14.0 dB` |
| **Ambient / Cinematic / Orchestral** | `-18.0` to `-14.0 LUFS` | `-1.5 dBTP` | `12.0–18.0 dB` | `<= -12.0 dB` |

## 3. Mandatory Quality Gates
- **True Peak Ceiling**: Must not exceed `ceiling_db + 0.05 dBTP` (default `-1.0 dBTP`) to prevent inter-sample clipping in AAC/MP3/Opus transcoders.
- **Crest Factor Guardrail**:
  - `< 6.0 dB`: Over-limited / crushed transients — back off limiter threshold or lengthen compressor attack (`20–35 ms`).
  - `> 16.0 dB` (non-ambient): Under-glued dynamics — apply `1.5–2.5 dB` bus compression (`2:1`, slow attack, auto release).
- **Phase & Mono Compatibility**:
  - Stereo correlation `corr` must stay `>= 0.20`.
  - Mono fold-down loss `mono_loss_db` must stay `>= -3.0 dB`.
  - Low-frequency side energy `low_side_db` (`< 120 Hz`) must stay `<= -14.0 dB`.
- **DC Offset & Clipping**: Zero flat-top clipped sample triplets (`clipped == 0`) and DC offset `< 0.002`.

